=================================================================
WEEK 2 – COMPLETE GIT COMMANDS

1. BASIC GIT COMMANDS

git --version
Description: Displays the installed Git version.

git config --global user.name "Your Name"
Description: Sets the global Git username.

git config --global user.email "youremail@gmail.com"
Description: Sets the global Git email.

git config --list
Description: Displays all Git configuration settings.

2. REPOSITORY MANAGEMENT

git init
Description: Initializes a new Git repository in the current folder.

git clone https://github.com/username/repository.git
Description: Copies a remote repository to the local computer.

git remote -v
Description: Displays connected remote repositories and their URLs.

git remote add origin https://github.com/username/repository.git
Description: Adds a remote repository named origin.

git remote remove origin
Description: Removes the remote named origin.

git remote rename origin upstream
Description: Renames the remote from origin to upstream.

git remote set-url origin https://github.com/username/new-repository.git
Description: Changes the URL of the remote repository.

git remote show origin
Description: Displays detailed information about the remote repository.

3. STAGING AND COMMITTING

git status
Description: Displays the current status of files.

git add filename.txt
Description: Adds a specific file to the staging area.

git add .
Description: Adds all changes to the staging area.

git commit -m "Initial commit"
Description: Saves staged changes with a commit message.

4. BRANCHING AND MERGING

git branch
Description: Lists all local branches.

git branch -a
Description: Lists all local and remote branches.

git branch -r
Description: Lists remote branches only.

git branch feature
Description: Creates a new branch named feature.

git checkout main
Description: Switches to the main branch.

git checkout feature
Description: Switches to the feature branch.

git checkout -b feature
Description: Creates and switches to a new branch.

git switch main
Description: Switches to the main branch.

git switch -c feature
Description: Creates and switches to a new branch.

git branch -d feature
Description: Safely deletes a merged branch.

git branch -D feature
Description: Force-deletes a branch even if it is not merged.

git branch --merged
Description: Lists branches already merged into the current branch.

git branch -d feature-a feature-b feature-c
Description: Deletes multiple merged local branches.

git checkout main
git merge feature
Description: Switches to main and merges the feature branch into it.

git remote prune origin
Description: Removes outdated remote-tracking branch references.

git fetch origin feature-branch
Description: Fetches a specific branch from the remote repository.

git push --set-upstream origin feature-branch
Description: Pushes the branch and sets its upstream tracking branch.

git fetch origin
git rebase origin/main
Description: Fetches remote updates and rebases the current branch onto remote main.

5. REMOTE REPOSITORY COMMANDS

git push origin main
Description: Uploads local commits to the remote main branch.

git push -u origin main
Description: Pushes main and sets its upstream branch.

git pull origin main
Description: Downloads and merges remote main changes into the current branch.

git fetch origin
Description: Downloads remote updates without merging them.

6. UNDOING CHANGES

git restore filename.txt
Description: Discards unstaged changes in a file.

git restore --staged filename.txt
Description: Removes a file from staging without losing its working changes.

git reset filename.txt
Description: Unstages a file without deleting its changes.

git reset --soft HEAD~1
Description: Undoes the latest commit but keeps changes staged.

git reset --mixed HEAD~1
Description: Undoes the latest commit and keeps changes unstaged.

git reset --hard HEAD~1
Description: Removes the latest commit and its working changes.

git revert commit_hash
Description: Creates a new commit that reverses an earlier commit.

git commit --amend -m "Corrected commit message"
Description: Changes the latest commit message.

7. VIEWING HISTORY

git log
Description: Displays complete commit history.

git log --oneline
Description: Displays commit history in a short format.

git diff
Description: Displays unstaged changes.

git diff --staged
Description: Displays staged changes.

git show
Description: Displays details of the latest commit.

git show commit_hash
Description: Displays details of a specific commit.

git blame script.py
Description: Shows who modified each line of a file.

git blame -L 25,25 script.py
Description: Shows who last changed line 25 of script.py.

git reflog
Description: Displays recent HEAD movements and helps recover deleted branches.

git checkout -b feature-ui commit_hash
Description: Recreates a branch from a previous commit.

8. REMOVING SENSITIVE FILES FROM HISTORY

git filter-repo --path secrets.txt --invert-paths
Description: Removes secrets.txt from Git history. Revoke exposed API keys first. This command requires git-filter-repo to be installed.

git push --force --all origin
Description: Force-pushes rewritten branch histories to the remote. Coordinate with collaborators first.

git push --force --tags origin
Description: Force-pushes rewritten tags to the remote.

9. RESOLVING MERGE CONFLICTS

git status
Description: Identifies files with merge conflicts.

Open the conflicted file and remove the conflict markers:
<<<<<<< HEAD
=======
>>>>>>> feature

git add app.js
Description: Stages the resolved file.

git commit -m "Resolve merge conflict"
Description: Completes the merge if Git requires a merge commit.

10. GITIGNORE

touch .gitignore
Description: Creates a .gitignore file.

*.log
Description: Ignores all log files.

node_modules/
Description: Ignores the node_modules directory.

secret_file.txt
Description: Ignores a particular file.

temp/
Description: Ignores the temp directory.

*.bak
Description: Ignores all backup files.

folder/*
!folder/important_file.txt
Description: Ignores all files in folder except important_file.txt.

git status
Description: Checks repository status and ignored/untracked files.

11. GIT STASH

git stash
Description: Temporarily saves modified tracked files and cleans the working directory.

git stash list
Description: Lists all saved stashes.

git stash apply
Description: Restores the latest stash without deleting it.

git stash pop
Description: Restores and removes the latest stash.

git stash drop
Description: Deletes the latest stash.

git stash clear
Description: Deletes all saved stashes.

12. PUSHING A MULTI-FOLDER PROJECT TO GITHUB

git init
Description: Initializes Git in the project root folder.

git config --global user.name "Your Name"
Description: Sets Git username.

git config --global user.email "youremail@gmail.com"
Description: Sets Git email.

git remote add origin https://github.com/username/repository.git
Description: Connects the local project to GitHub.

git add .
Description: Stages all project files and folders.

git commit -m "Initial commit"
Description: Creates the first commit.

git branch -M main
Description: Renames the current branch to main.

git push -u origin main
Description: Uploads the project to GitHub and sets upstream tracking.

13. COMPLETE BASIC WORKFLOW

git init
git status
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/username/repository.git
git push -u origin main

Description: Initializes, stages, commits and uploads the project to GitHub.

14. COMPLETE REMOTE WORKFLOW

git clone https://github.com/username/repository.git
git remote -v
git pull origin main
git add .
git commit -m "Updated project"
git push origin main

Description: Clones a repository, checks its remote, downloads updates, commits changes and uploads them to GitHub.

15. COMPLETE BRANCH WORKFLOW

git checkout -b feature
git add .
git commit -m "Added feature"
git push -u origin feature
git checkout main
git merge feature
git push origin main
git branch -d feature

Description: Creates a feature branch, commits changes, pushes it, merges it into main and deletes the merged local branch.
